 &OCEAN_MODEL_NML
 TIME_TENDENCY   = twolevel                        ,
 IMPOSE_INIT_FROM_RESTART        = F,
 REINITIALIZE_THICKNESS  = F,
 BAROCLINIC_SPLIT        =           1,
 BAROTROPIC_SPLIT        =          80,
 SURFACE_HEIGHT_SPLIT    =           1,
 LAYOUT  =           6,           5,
 IO_LAYOUT       =           1,           5,
 DEBUG   = F,
 VERTICAL_COORDINATE     = geopotential                    ,
 DT_OCEAN        =        7200,
 CMIP_UNITS      = F
 /

 ==>Note: Running mom4 using    30 computer processors.

  
 ==>Note: Running mom4 with staggered twotime level scheme to compute time tende
 ncies.
          This is the default. Mass/volume and tracer are conserved with this sc
 heme.
  

 ==>Note: Time%Time_init = time stamp at very start of the mom4 experiment is given by
yyyy/mm/dd hh:mm:ss =  101/ 1/ 1  0: 0: 0

 ==>Note: Time%model_time = time stamp at start of this leg of the mom4 experiment is
yyyy/mm/dd hh:mm:ss =  103/ 1/ 1  0: 0: 0

 ==>Note: Time%init=.false. =>mom4 will start from restart conditions from previous leg of experiment.

 ==> Note: time steps (seconds) used for mom4
  dtts  (tracer)                            =    7200.00
  dtuv  (baroclinic)                        =    7200.00
  dteta (surface height or bottom pressure) =    7200.00
  dtbt  (barotropic)                        =      90.00

 ==> Note: The velocity equations will be split into baroclinic and barotropic pieces.


  ==> Note: Using mom4 with geopotential vertical coordinate.
      Beware of vanishing top model grid cells. 

     The equations are Boussinesq, and so conserve volume rather than mass.
     Use one of the pressure-like coordinates to get non-Boussinesq effects.



 &OCEAN_GRIDS_NML
 DEBUG_THIS_MODULE       = T,
 VERBOSE_INIT    = T,
 READ_RHO0_PROFILE       = F,
 WRITE_GRID      = F
 /
